# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for the macos-asan build
# (CMakePresets.json, tests/README.md): the known findings that are not fixed
# in the macOS port. Only third-party or system code, and findings in the
# game's shared code that are filed upstream, go here; Mac-only code
# (CANE_GL41 blocks, Sly1-Release/gl41, platform/ __APPLE__ paths, tests/) is
# fixed, never suppressed. Every entry names the check and the narrowest
# function, with the reason above it. Format: <check>:<function or file pattern>
# (a pattern matches any part of the name; * is a wildcard, ^ and $ anchor
# it to the start and end of the name). Each entry was
# checked by re-running the suite: without the file the report appears, with it
# not. None of the suppressed functions contains a CANE_GL41 block (sw.cpp,
# sound.cpp, spaprops.cpp, lo.cpp, find.cpp and brx.cpp have none; alo.cpp has
# some, but none inside PostAloLoad), so these entries cannot hide a report
# from Mac-only code. A pattern is matched against the symbolized name, which
# carries the parameter list ("PostAloLoad(ALO*)"), so "^Name(" matches that
# function only and not every function whose name starts with it.
#
# --- Third-party and system code: none so far (GLFW, imgui, glad and FAudio are
# --- instrumented; SDL2, FFmpeg and the Apple GL driver are not, and ASan's
# --- interceptors reported nothing through them).
#
# --- Known findings in the game's shared code (not Mac-only; not fixed in the
# --- macOS port). Each is filed upstream as the issue given; remove the entry
# --- when the upstream fix lands. Matched by function name.
#
# theclub654/ProjectCane#66: enum MUSID (spaprops.h) has no fixed underlying
# type and ends at MUSID_Max = 16, so its valid range is -32..31, but the
# retail music ids parsed from the world's "MUSID_xx.mus" name (sw.cpp,
# LoadSwFromBrx) are MUSID_34..MUSID_68 (0x34..0x68). Every load of such a
# MUSID is undefined behaviour.
enum:LoadSwFromBrx
enum:StartMusidSong
enum:PreloadMusidSong
enum:FindMusicBank
enum:TraceMusicEvent
enum:UnloadMusic
# theclub654/ProjectCane#67: enum OPTID (spaprops.h) declares only
# OPTID_Nil = -1 (valid range -1..0), but the CUSTOM_*_PROPERTY option thunks
# carry option ids around 1176..1186 from the level data through it.
enum:RefThunkLoCUSTOM_*_PROPERTY
enum:EnsureLoSidebag*
# theclub654/ProjectCane#68: PdlFromSwOid (find.cpp) hashes with a signed int
# multiply, oid * 0x95675, which overflows for most object ids.
signed-integer-overflow:PdlFromSwOid
# theclub654/ProjectCane#69: PostAloLoad (alo.cpp) advances the child-list
# iterator past the null end of the list ((uint8_t*)nullptr + m_ibDle) before
# the loop test. Anchored so it does not also hide PostAloLoadCallback.
pointer-overflow:^PostAloLoad(
# theclub654/ProjectCane#58: LoadOptionFromBrx (brx.cpp) stores
# OTYP_Oid/Cid/... options as a 4-byte int32 into fields declared short
# (CAMERA::oidTarget, EXPLS::oidRender/oidNextRender/oidTouch,
# RCHM::oidHost/oidTouch), misaligned for some and overwriting the next field:
# another short, or the low two bytes of CAMERA::ppntTarget (data corruption,
# see the issue).
alignment:LoadOptionFromBrx
